  "clues": [
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "It was a giant tortoise.",
      "tags": [
        "giant_tortoise"
      ],
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "habitat",
      "text": "It lived on Pinta Island in the Galápagos.",
      "tags": [
        "pinta_island"
      ],
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "conservation",
      "text": "Sailors hunted it, and goats brought to the island ate the plants it needed.",
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "conservation",
      "text": "The last one, Lonesome George, died on 24 June 2012 after 40 years in captivity.",
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "It had five claws on each front foot.",
      "tags": [
        "five_front_claws"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gal%C3%A1pagos_tortoise"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Its shell was a 'saddleback': raised high at the front, above the neck.",
      "tags": [
        "saddleback_shell"
      ],
      "source": "literature",
      "url": "https://www.reptilesofecuador.com/chelonoidis_abingdonii.html"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "It had a patch of contrasting color on its throat.",
      "tags": [
        "throat_patch"
      ],
      "source": "literature",
      "url": "https://iucn-tftsg.org/wp-content/uploads/file/Articles/Van_Denburgh_1914.pdf"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "As an adult, it had no teeth at all.",
      "tags": [
        "toothless"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/galapagos-giant-tortoise"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It often rested in the sun to warm its body.",
      "tags": [
        "basker"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/galapagos-giant-tortoise"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It found most of its food on the ground.",
      "tags": [
        "feeds_on_ground"
      ],
      "source": "literature",
      "url": "https://www.reptilesofecuador.com/chelonoidis_abingdonii.html"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It made a loud hissing sound.",
      "tags": [
        "hisses"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/galapagostortoises/behavior"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It made loud calls that carried far, such as roars or bellows.",
      "tags": [
        "loud_calls"
      ],
      "source": "literature",
      "url": "https://www.reptilesofecuador.com/chelonoidis_abingdonii.html"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It could go days or longer without drinking, getting most of its water from its food.",
      "tags": [
        "rarely_drinks"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gal%C3%A1pagos_tortoise"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It spread plant seeds to new places by eating them, often in fruit, and passing them in its droppings.",
      "tags": [
        "seed_spreader"
      ],
      "source": "ngo"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It moved very slowly, even when disturbed.",
      "tags": [
        "slow_mover"
      ],
      "source": "literature",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15802673/"
    },
    {
      "category": "reproduction",
      "text": "It laid its eggs out of the water, on land or underground.",
      "tags": [
        "eggs_on_land"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/galapagos-giant-tortoise"
    },
    {
      "category": "reproduction",
      "text": "Whether its eggs hatched as males or females depended on how warm the nest was.",
      "tags": [
        "temperature_sex"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/galapagos-giant-tortoise"
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "Lonesome George became a world-famous symbol of extinction.",
      "source": "ngo"
    },
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "Tortoises with some Pinta ancestry were found on another island, so a little of its family line survives.",
      "source": "news"
    }
  ],
